# Internationalization (en / fr)

**Always translate all user-facing strings** when adding or changing UI copy, API validation/permission messages, or choice enum labels. Supported locales: **English (`en`)** and **French (`fr`)**.

## Where strings live

| String type | Owner | Mechanism |
|-------------|-------|-----------|
| Choice enum `title`, user-facing API errors | Backend | `gettext_lazy` / `gettext` + `backend/locale/{en,fr}/LC_MESSAGES/` |
| Flutter UI chrome | Mobile | ARB in `mobile/lib/l10n/` (`AppLocalizations`) |
| Angular UI chrome | Web | JSON catalogs in `web/public/assets/i18n/{en,fr}.json` + `LocaleService` / `t` pipe |

## Rules

- Do **not** ship hardcoded English-only user-facing UI or untranslated API messages/choice labels.
- Keep `value` / `css` on choice enums language-independent; never invent client-side title maps for API enums.
- Clients must send `Accept-Language` so Django `LocaleMiddleware` can localize API copy.
- User-generated content (org names, descriptions, notes) is not translated.
- When touching an existing English-only string, migrate it into the correct catalog at the same time.
- After backend string changes: update `.po`, run `compilemessages`, and cover with a translation test when practical.
